vector<array<int,2>> V(100001, {-1, -1}); // works well

vector<vector<int> V(100001,vector<int>(2,-1));// cause tle 

Key Concept
array<int,2>
Fixed size (2)
Stored inside vector directly
No extra memory allocation


vector<int>(2)
Dynamic size
Needs separate memory allocation
Happens 100001 times


🚀 When to Use What
✅ Use vector<array<int,2>>
Fixed size (like 2, 3, 4)
Performance matters (CP, interviews)
❌ Avoid vector<vector<int>>
When inner size is small and fixed
When n is large (1e5+)
